    {
      "id": "wifi",
      "chapter": "Myth 1: Wi-Fi is the internet",
      "narration": "Many people say the internet is down when their Wi-Fi drops. But Wi-Fi only covers the last few metres, from your router to your device. The router then connects to your provider, and your provider connects to the rest of the world. So when the Wi-Fi fails, the internet is usually fine. Only your link to it is broken.",
