      "id": "sky",
      "chapter": "Myth 2: the internet is in the sky",
      "narration": "It feels wireless, so people imagine satellites carrying it. In fact, almost all traffic between continents travels through cables on the ocean floor. More than a million kilometres of them, each about as thick as a garden hose. Satellites carry only a small share.",
