      "id": "cloud",
      "chapter": "Myth 4: the cloud is somewhere above us",
      "narration": "Your photos are not floating in the air. The cloud is simply someone else's computers, packed into huge buildings called data centres. When you save a file to the cloud, it goes to a real hard drive, in a real building, somewhere in the world.",
